# Earthbend's delayed "When that land dies or is put into exile, return it to the battlefield tapped under your control"
# (CR 701.66a) waits only for that land: going to a hand is neither dying nor being exiled (the card's ruling: "it will
# not be returned"), and the card in hand is a new object it can never trigger for (CR 400.7, 603.7c). Bot1's Badgermole
# Cub earthbends its Forest (a 1/1 land creature); Bot1 returns the Forest to its hand with Unsummon. The Forest stays
# in Bot1's hand, and by Bot2's turn the delayed ability, which can never trigger, is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Badgermole Cub
Mox Sapphire
Unsummon
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

